### Invocation protocol
1. Task received → identify domain(s)
2. Spawn all agents from that domain as **parallel subagents**
3. Each subagent reads: own `.md` + `AGENT_CONTEXT.md` + relevant context file
4. Collect outputs → resolve conflicts → unified response to user
5. Update `AGENT_CONTEXT.md` at end of session

### Communication between agents (async via files)
<% if (modules.backend) { -%>
- Backend writes API contracts → `.claude/context/api-spec.md`
<% } -%>
<% if (modules.mobile || modules.web) { -%>
- Frontend reads contracts → builds against spec, never assumptions
<% } -%>
<% if (integrations.cicd) { -%>
- CICD writes resource state → `.claude/context/infra-state.md`
<% } -%>
- QA writes test results → `.claude/context/test-report.md`
- Analyzer writes findings → `.claude/context/analysis-report.md`
- Security reads everything flagged, writes findings inline with severity tags

### When to invoke Security agent
Always spawn Security alongside other agents when task touches:
- Any auth endpoint or JWT handling
<% if (integrations.aws) { -%>
- New IAM role, SSM parameter, or secret
<% } -%>
- New third-party package/dependency
<% if (integrations.aws) { -%>
- S3 upload or user-generated content
- Any change to EC2 security groups or RDS access
<% } -%>
- User data changes affecting privacy/compliance

